Z||000002||Ayrow||12-18-2001||12:12 AM||||I think the price is way too high if you ask me (which you did, sorta).<P>I saw an '87 Blue GT (just like yours and mine) go for $2500 on E-bay about a month ago.<BR>Let's not forget that '85 you're looking at  has been painted over twice.<BR>You might want to think twice and make sure it has not been hit.<P>Send me the VIN# and I will do a Carfax check on it for you if you like.<P>If that were an '88, then maybe the price would be more realistic.<P>Good Luck,<P>Ayrow <A HREF="http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html</A> ||||reg||13
Z||000003||RossT||12-18-2001||12:49 AM||||Cool... As you may or may not know, I too have one of those ultra low mileage gt's.  The kind you really don't want to drive too much.  The best thing I ever did was buy a backup (daily driver) fiero about 2 months ago!!  You can get your fiero fix everyday, well almost every day (winter can damper things).  My advice is to don't jump on the first car you find, unless its a great deal!!<BR>I found a yellow 88 formula with 32,000 miles for $4,000.  So there are good deals out there, just keep your eyes open.  Best of all, you get to search the tech section over and over again.  Something we didn't have to do with are low mileage cars!!<P>good luck||||reg||1
