Z||000009||RRobinson||12-18-2001||12:23 PM||||Cool,<BR>I agree the price seems high for an 85 SE on it's third paint job. Mileage?<P>I quite like my slushbox 88 GT. It's kind of nice not to have to shift in traffic for a change. For a daily driver, it's not a bad choice. <P>RR <BR>2-88 GTs<BR>2-87 GTs<BR>87 SE V6 <BR>86 GT 5-Speed<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||12-18-2001||01:02 PM||||Price is a little high, but it really depends on the condition of the car.<BR>Also, a V-6 85 SE is not terribly common. (I don't know how <I>uncommon</I> it is, however.) <BR>I have slushboxes in both of my 88s. Kinda nice in traffic. <BR>Count on replacing (or at least having to unplug) your TCC solenoid, if it hasn't been done already. This solenoid has "gone south" on every automatic Fiero I've owned.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
